<appendix xml:id="sec-statistics-and-parameters" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Symbols, formulas, statistics and parameters</title>

  <section xml:id="sec-app-symbols-and-standard-errors">
    <title>Symbols and standard errors</title>
    <idx><h>Mean</h><h>of a population</h></idx>
    <idx><h>Mean</h><h>of a sample</h></idx>
    <idx><h>Mean difference</h><h>between</h></idx>
    <idx>Mean difference</idx>
    <idx><h>Proportions</h><h>of a population</h></idx>
    <idx><h>Proportions</h><h>of a sample</h></idx>
    <idx>Odds ratio</idx>
    <idx><h>Regression</h><h>coefficients</h></idx>
    <idx>Correlation coefficient (Pearson)</idx>
    <idx>Symbols used</idx>

    <ul>
      <li><p>Table <xref ref="tab-parameters-statistics"/> lists the statistics used to estimate unknown population parameters.</p></li>
      <li><p>When the sampling distribution is approximately normally distributed, under appropriate statistical validity conditions, this is indicated by&#160;&#10004;.<idx>Sampling distribution</idx></p></li>
      <li>
        <p>The value of the mean of the sampling distribution (the <em>sampling mean</em>) is<idx>Sampling mean</idx>:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><p>unknown, for <em>confidence intervals</em>.</p></li>
          <li><p>assumed to be the value given in the null hypothesis, for <em>hypothesis tests</em>.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

